        {
          "title": "Present perfect o past simple",
          "head": [
            "",
            "Present perfect",
            "Past simple"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "¿Cuándo?",
              "no se dice o no importa",
              "momento concreto y terminado"
            ],
            [
              "Marcadores",
              "ever, never, already, yet, just, so far",
              "yesterday, last week, in 2019, … ago, When…?"
            ],
            [
              "Ejemplo",
              "I'**ve been** to Italy three times.",
              "I **went** to Italy last summer."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "exceptions": [
        "*been* y *gone*: *She **has been** to London* = ha estado y ya volvió; *She **has gone** to London* = se ha ido y sigue allí.",
        "*already* y *just* van entre *have* y el participio (*I've **just** eaten*); *yet* va al final y solo en negativas y preguntas (*Have you finished **yet**?*).",
        "Con *this morning / today / this week* puedes usar present perfect si ese periodo **no ha terminado**: *I've had three coffees today.*"
      ],
      "practice": [
        {
          "q": "___ you ever ___ (try) Indian food?",
          "a": "Have … tried"
        },
        {
          "q": "I ___ (never / eat) oysters.",
          "a": "have never eaten"
        },
        {
          "q": "She ___ (go) to the supermarket. She'll be back soon.",
          "a": "has gone"
        },
        {
          "q": "We ___ (have) lunch at 2 yesterday.",
          "a": "had",
          "why": "*yesterday* → past simple"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "present-perfect-continuous",
      "title": "Present perfect continuous",
      "title_es": "Llevar tiempo haciendo algo",
      "use": "Para acciones que **empezaron en el pasado y siguen ahora**. Equivale a «llevar… haciendo». Se pregunta con *How long…?* y se responde con *for* (periodo) o *since* (desde un momento).",
      "forms": [
        {
          "label": "Afirmativa",
          "pattern": "sujeto + have / has been + verbo-ing",
          "example": "I have been working here for 9 years."
        },
        {
          "label": "Pregunta",
          "pattern": "How long + have / has + sujeto + been + verbo-ing?",
          "example": "How long have you been working at the EOI?"
        }
      ],
      "keywords": [
        "How long…?",
        "for",
        "since"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "How long have you been working at the EOI?",
          "es": "¿Cuánto tiempo llevas trabajando en la EOI?"
        },
        {
          "en": "I have been working at the EOI for 9 years.",
          "es": "Llevo 9 años trabajando en la EOI."
        },
        {
          "en": "She's been learning English since September.",
          "es": "Está aprendiendo inglés desde septiembre."
        }
      ],
      "mistakes": [
        {
          "wrong": "I am working here for 9 years.",
          "right": "I have been working here for 9 years.",
          "why": "Para «llevar tiempo haciendo algo» no se usa el presente."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "I've been living here since 3 years.",
          "right": "I've been living here for 3 years.",
          "why": "*for* + periodo (3 years); *since* + punto de inicio (2021, Monday)."
        }
      ],
      "tables": [
        {
          "title": "*for* o *since*",
          "head": [
            "for + periodo",
            "since + punto de inicio"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "for **9 years**",
              "since **2017**"
            ],
            [
              "for **two weeks**",
              "since **last Monday**"
            ],
            [
              "for **a long time**",
              "since **I was a child**"
            ],
            [
              "for **ages**",
              "since **September**"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "exceptions": [
        "Con **verbos de estado** se usa present perfect **simple**, no continuo: *I've **known** him for years* (no *I've been knowing*).",
        "*How long have you lived here?* y *How long have you been living here?* significan casi lo mismo con *live, work, study*."
      ],
      "practice": [
        {
          "q": "I ___ (learn) English since 2020.",
          "a": "have been learning"
        },
        {
          "q": "She's been working here ___ six months.",
          "a": "for"
        },
        {
          "q": "We've been waiting ___ ten o'clock.",
          "a": "since"
        },
        {
          "q": "How long ___ you ___ (know) Ana?",
          "a": "have … known",
          "why": "*know* es de estado."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "going-to",
      "title": "Going to",
      "title_es": "Planes futuros",
      "use": "Para **planes e intenciones** que ya has decidido, y para predicciones cuando ves que algo va a pasar.",
      "forms": [
        {
          "label": "Afirmativa",
          "pattern": "sujeto + am / is / are + going to + infinitivo",
          "example": "I'm going to cook tonight."
        },
        {
          "label": "Negativa",
          "pattern": "sujeto + 'm not / isn't / aren't + going to + infinitivo",
          "example": "I'm not going to eat dessert."
        },
        {
          "label": "Pregunta",
          "pattern": "Am / Is / Are + sujeto + going to + infinitivo?",
          "example": "Are you going to eat dessert?"
        }
      ],
      "keywords": [
        "tonight",
        "tomorrow",
        "next week",
        "this summer"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "Are you going to eat dessert?",
          "es": "¿Vas a tomar postre?"
        },
        {
          "en": "No, I'm not going to eat dessert.",
          "es": "No, no voy a tomar postre."
        },
        {
          "en": "Look at those clouds! It's going to rain.",
          "es": "¡Mira esas nubes! Va a llover."
        }
      ],
      "mistakes": [
        {
          "wrong": "I going to cook pasta.",
          "right": "I'm going to cook pasta.",
          "why": "No olvides el verbo *be* (*am / is / are*)."
        }
      ],
      "tables": [
        {
          "title": "Futuro en B1: ¿cuál uso?",
          "head": [
            "Forma",
            "Uso",
            "Ejemplo"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "going to",
              "intención o plan decidido; predicción con pruebas",
              "I'**m going to** cook paella tonight. / Look at those clouds! It'**s going to** rain."
            ],
            [
              "present continuous",
              "plan ya organizado (hora, sitio)",
              "I'**m meeting** Ana at 8."
            ],
            [
              "will",
              "decisión en el momento, promesa, predicción sin pruebas",
              "I'**ll have** the fish, please. / I think it **will** be sunny."
            ],
            [
              "present simple",
              "horarios",
              "The train **leaves** at 6."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "exceptions": [
        "Con *go* se suele decir *I'm going to the cinema* (presente continuo) en vez de *I'm going to go to the cinema*, aunque las dos son correctas."
      ],
      "practice": [
        {
          "q": "Look at that man! He ___ (fall).",
          "a": "is going to fall",
          "why": "Predicción con pruebas."
        },
        {
          "q": "I ___ (not / eat) dessert tonight. I'm on a diet.",
          "a": "'m not going to eat"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "past-simple",
      "title": "Past simple",
      "title_es": "Pasado simple",
      "use": "Para acciones **terminadas en un momento concreto** del pasado: *yesterday*, *last week*, *in 2019*, *five years ago*.",
      "forms": [
        {
          "label": "Afirmativa",
          "pattern": "sujeto + verbo en pasado (-ed o irregular)",
          "example": "I met him 5 years ago."
        },
        {
          "label": "Negativa",
          "pattern": "sujeto + didn't + infinitivo",
          "example": "I didn't meet him at work."
        },
        {
          "label": "Pregunta",
          "pattern": "(Wh-) + did + sujeto + infinitivo?",
          "example": "When did you meet him?"
        },
        {
          "label": "Verbo be",
          "pattern": "was / were",
          "example": "Where were you yesterday?"
        }
      ],
      "keywords": [
        "yesterday",
        "last…",
        "… ago",
        "in 2019",
        "When…?"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "Where were you yesterday? — I was at home.",
          "es": "¿Dónde estuviste ayer? — Estuve en casa."
        },
        {
          "en": "When did you meet him? — I met him 5 years ago.",
          "es": "¿Cuándo lo conociste? — Lo conocí hace 5 años."
        }
      ],
      "mistakes": [
        {
          "wrong": "When did you met him?",
          "right": "When did you meet him?",
          "why": "Después de *did* el verbo va en infinitivo."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "I met him ago 5 years.",
          "right": "I met him 5 years ago.",
          "why": "*ago* va detrás del periodo de tiempo."
        }
      ],
      "tables": [
        {
          "title": "Pronunciación de -ed en verbos regulares",
          "head": [
            "Sonido",
            "Cuándo",
            "Ejemplos"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "/t/",
              "después de /p, k, f, s, ʃ, tʃ/",
              "cooked, washed, watched, baked"
            ],
            [
              "/d/",
              "después de vocal y otros sonidos sonoros",
              "played, boiled, grilled, steamed"
            ],
            [
              "/ɪd/",
              "después de /t/ o /d/ (se añade una sílaba)",
              "wanted, needed, roasted, waited"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "exceptions": [
        "Con *was / were* no se usa *did*: *Where **were** you?* (no *Where did you be?*).",
        "Ortografía: *stop → stopped*, *study → studied*, *play → played*, *fry → fried*."
      ],
      "practice": [
        {
          "q": "When ___ you ___ (meet) him?",
          "a": "did … meet"
        },
        {
          "q": "I ___ (not / go) out last night.",
          "a": "didn't go"
        },
        {
          "q": "They ___ (be) at home yesterday.",
          "a": "were"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
